# 18ai — agent conventions

## New slice / chat

- Attach `docs/architecture.md` and the slice plan (e.g. under `~/.cursor/plans/`) at the start of implementation work.
- Engine changes: run `npm test -w engine` (and `npm run typecheck -w engine` when touching types) before treating work as done.

## TypeScript layout

- **Types only**: Do not put classes, runtime values, or large `const` data in the same file as interfaces/types. Keep `*-types.ts` (or `map-types.ts`) type-only.
- **Large static data**: Own file (e.g. `map-manifest-seed.ts`). Import from a small module that exports the public shape (e.g. `Map.map`).
- **Seed / manifest rows**: Prefer **one compact object per line** (single-line records), not one property per line, unless readability truly breaks down.

## Engine data model

- Prefer **`HexSlotWithoutCoords`** (or equivalent `Omit<…, 'q' | 'r'>` from `HexSlot`) for manifest seeds instead of a parallel hand-maintained union.
- Hydration naming: e.g. **`hydrateHexCoords`** / static helpers on a small **`Map`** class are fine; when importing that class in app code, **alias** it (e.g. `Map as ChesapeakeMap`) so it does not shadow the global `Map`.

## Comments and docs pointers

- **Do not** use inline or block comments that cite `docs/architecture.md`, `resources/`, or paths under `resources/` (including `static-board.html`). Design docs stay out of code comments.
- **Hex / grid math** in comments: point to **Red Blob Games** (e.g. axial → pixel `#hex-to-pixel-axial`, size/spacing `#size-and-spacing`) instead of internal docs.

## Scope and style

- Match existing naming, imports (`*.js` suffix in engine ESM), and file placement; minimal diffs unless the slice requires broader edits.
- Prefer complete sentences in commit/PR text; keep user-facing copy free of doc-path name-drops unless the product intentionally links there.
